{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Benchmarks"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"See how FirebladeECS revisions compare on a shared workload suite, and run the comparison yourself."}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/benchmarks"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The benchmark suite measures the same workloads at several committed FirebladeECS revisions, such as a release tag against ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"main"},{"text":". The workloads cover entity creation, destruction and lookup, adding and removing components, iterating families, system updates and component events. Revisions with value-type components run each workload on both the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"archetype"},{"text":" and the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sparseSet"},{"text":" storage (see ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","isActive":true},{"text":"), so a report also shows what the storage choice costs.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"How-results-are-made-trustworthy","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"How results are made trustworthy"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each revision is built once and measured in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"text":" independent process replicates, interleaved in a seeded random order. The replicate is the unit of analysis: the centre value is the median of the replicate medians, with a distribution-free order-statistic 95% confidence interval. A speed-up against the baseline is the Hodges–Lehmann estimate with its exact confidence interval, tested with an exact Mann–Whitney test and adjusted across all comparisons of a report with Benjamini–Hochberg. A change counts as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"faster"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"slower"},{"text":" only when it is significant and clears the ±5% equivalence zone; an interval inside that zone is reported as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"equivalent"},{"text":", anything else as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inconclusive"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Read-and-reproduce","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Read and reproduce"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The first published report comes with the 2.0.0 release."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The statistical design and workload parity notes: "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/fireblade-engine\/ecs\/blob\/main\/Documentation\/Benchmarks\/Methodology.md","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To measure revisions locally, pass comma-separated tags, branches or commit IDs. Results are saved under ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Benchmarks\/Results\/<UTC timestamp>\/"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["make benchmark-compare REFS=1.4.3,main REPLICATES=10 BENCHMARK_FILTER='.*'","make benchmark-report RESULTS=\"Benchmarks\/Results\/<run>\/*.json\" REPORT_BASELINE=1.4.3"],"syntax":"sh","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Without ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BENCHMARK_FILTER"},{"text":" only 16 entities of every workload plus ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entity.create.no-entities"},{"text":" (which only has 0 entities) run. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"make benchmark-report"},{"text":" renders the single file ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BenchmarkReport.html"},{"text":" from saved results and never runs benchmarks. See ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Benchmarks\/README.md"},{"text":" for all options.","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"],"generated":true}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/SavingAndLoadingScenes":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","role":"article","title":"Saving and Loading Scenes","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/savingandloadingscenes","abstract":[{"text":"Store a whole ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","type":"reference"},{"text":" on disk and load it again with the same entities, components and entity identifiers.","type":"text"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StorageKind"}],"title":"Nexus.StorageKind","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind","abstract":[{"text":"The storage a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","type":"reference"},{"text":" keeps its entities and components in.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StorageKind","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS":{"type":"topic","title":"Getting started with Fireblade ECS","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/gettingstartedwithfirebladeecs","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn the API and key types Fireblade provides to compose your game or app logic."}],"kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A lightweight, fast and easy to use Entity-Component System in Swift."}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS","title":"FirebladeECS","role":"collection"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/MigratingToFirebladeECS2":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/migratingtofirebladeecs2","abstract":[{"text":"Move a project from FirebladeECS 1.x to 2.0: components become value types, and every write goes through the nexus.","type":"text"}],"title":"Migrating to FirebladeECS 2","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEventMask":{"url":"\/documentati